# p-drag-out (h11-p-drag): P dragged past the canvas's right edge (1423) and
# past the 1440 viewport's edge out to x=1500 and held: P keeps following
# (the canvas's pointer capture retargets the moves on every target; p=11.44
# in WebKit and Chromium), the camera unchanged, the closed hand with P's
# drop line out. Ends held; the release past the edge still ends the drag
# (probed: the modes cleared, the cursor pan), but its hover state is
# lag-divergent by construction, so no release read belongs to this state.
# Firefox's past-edge coordinates are broken by the engine (h7-fix-capture):
# it delivers garbage coordinates for the move, so the reference reads
# p=-18.56 there and the port must equal the reference, not WebKit.
# Behaviour (read on ref-h11 at c6754e7): cursor grab-active; the p line
# 11.44 in WebKit and Chromium, -18.56 in Firefox.
size 1440 900
density 2
scheme dark
mode dark
theme arctic-ice
wait 500
move 1028 290
wait 200
down
wait 150
move 1500 290 over 160
wait 300
shot p-drag-out
up
